<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How fast is Mbappé in mph?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Kylian Mbappé's career-best recorded top speed is 38 km/h, which converts to approximately 23.6 mph. This figure was set around 2019 during his PSG era. His current 2025-26 season speeds are closer to 35 to 36 km/h (21.7 to 22.4 mph) based on La Liga and Champions League tracking data. He is still among the fastest players in the world, though not leading the 2026 World Cup speed charts based on available data.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How fast is Haaland in mph?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Erling Haaland has been clocked at 36.5 km/h (22.7 mph) at the 2026 World Cup. What makes this remarkable is that he is 6 feet 4 inches tall and weighs approximately 194 pounds — a body type that should, theoretically, sacrifice some top-end speed for physical presence. That he matches fast wingers in top speed while being built like a center-back is one of the most unusual physical profiles in elite soccer.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Who is the fastest player at the 2026 World Cup?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Based on early tournament tracking data, Australian defender Jordan Bos is the fastest player recorded at the 2026 World Cup with 36.7 km/h (22.8 mph) during Australia's opening win over Turkey. Haaland and Uzbekistan's Khusanov share second at 36.5 km/h (22.7 mph). These numbers will continue to be updated as the knockout rounds produce more high-intensity sprint situations.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How fast is the average person compared to World Cup players?</div>
<div class="faq-a">The average untrained adult reaches approximately 8 to 10 mph at maximum effort. A fit recreational athlete might hit 12 to 15 mph. High school varsity athletes average 14 to 18 mph. The fastest World Cup players sprint at 22 to 23.6 mph — roughly 2 to 3 times faster than an average adult. Use our <a href="https://athletecalculator.com/sprint-speed-calculator">Sprint Speed Calculator</a> to see exactly where your speed ranks. Full context on <a href="https://athletecalculator.com/how-fast-is-the-average-person">average human sprint speeds by age and group</a> is also available.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Are World Cup players faster than NFL players?</div>
<div class="faq-a">In terms of raw top-end speed, the fastest World Cup players appear to be at or slightly above the fastest NFL players. The fastest NFL combine 40-yard dash on record corresponds to approximately 21.8 mph. The top World Cup sprinters reach 22.7 to 23.6 mph. However, the 40-yard dash measures a short-distance acceleration from a standing start, while soccer top speeds are recorded in open-field match conditions at full stride — making direct comparison difficult. See our <a href="https://athletecalculator.com/average-40-yard-dash-times">40-yard dash averages guide</a> for full NFL combine speed context.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How fast is Usain Bolt compared to soccer players?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Usain Bolt's world record peak speed during his 9.58-second 100m world record was 44.72 km/h (27.8 mph). The fastest soccer players at the 2026 World Cup reach approximately 36.5 to 38 km/h (22.7 to 23.6 mph). Bolt is roughly 4 to 5 mph faster than the fastest soccer player ever recorded at top speed. However, Bolt was running on a track, in sprinting spikes, with a full running start, having trained exclusively for maximum sprint velocity. Soccer players reach their speeds in match conditions, in cleats, having already run several miles, often while controlling or chasing a ball. The contexts are very different.</div>
</div>
